  "question": {
    "text": "A is an optically inactive alkyl chloride which on reaction with aqueous $\\mathrm{KOH}$ gives $\\mathrm{B}$. $\\mathrm{B}$ on heating with $\\mathrm{Cu}$ at $300^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ gives an alkene $\\mathrm{C}$, what are $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$",
